00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.470
Uneasiness, and Cell Phones

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:53.850
Asu!

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.020
W-Why do we have these?

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.620
There was a raffle in the shopping district today.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.040
These are real, right, Onee-chan?

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.650
Onee-chan?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.110
Cell… Phones?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.800
A cell phone means you can carry with you, right?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:14.240
I’ve always thought that these were mystical devices that only existed in fantasies and stories!{I’d always thought they were things found only in stories of distant, faraway worlds, completely separate from our own…}

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.170
No, you’re exaggerating too much…

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.390
Hey, is this a dream?!

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:18.920
I-I don’t think so.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.110
Well then,

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.320
I wonder how you’re supposed to use them.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.580
Let’s see. To turn it on, you’re supposed to press…

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.610
Is it here?

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:28.300
Where, where?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.680
After that,

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:36.140
um, the prepaid plan gives us 3000 yen worth of minutes to use in three months.{Then you choose the payment method. This card has 3000 yen and works for three months.}

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.480
3000 yen worth?{ARGH ARGH ARGH}

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.480
Hey, look at the next part.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.540
“Enter the number, and…”

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.550
And after that…

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.530
I wonder if they’re ready to use now.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.660
Onee-chan, try calling me.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.220
O-Okay.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.100
It’s ringing!{why do they have dead zombie eyes in this scene}

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.730
Hello!

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.260
Hello.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.880
Is that how it’s supposed to go?

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.020
Did you hang up?

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.650
That was a close call!{Hale, you should be very proud of this pun!}

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:12.450
What was?

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.660
We have a limited number of minutes to use on these!

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.350
3000 yen worth. We should only use them for important stuff.{FUCK YOU, SCENE CHANGE}

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.160
Oh, I suppose you’re right.{9 YEAR OLD ENGLISH RIGHT HERE}

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.230
Onee-chan, are you okay?

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.470
Looks like I was doing it again, huh? Yes, I’m fine!

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:39.240
Plus, starting from today, we have these, right?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.580
Tada!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.660
If anything happens, call me right away, okay?

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.800
You too, Onee-chan.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.060
Well then, I’m off!

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.860
<i>I’m really tired again today.</i>

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.460
I forgot to thank her again,

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.940
even though the tofu-miso soup was so wonderful.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.490
Oh, that’s right. I need to turn my phone off while I’m in class.{perhaps "during the school day"}

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.740
Hey, what are you doing?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.550
Ginko-chan, good morning.{sigh. Name then greeting still sounds weird to me}

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.480
Good morning.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.400
What? You bought a cell phone?!

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.340
This? No, I won it in a raffle in the shopping district.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.280
A raffle…

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:33.000
My sister has a phone too, and it’s much fancier and nicer than this one, just so you know!

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.180
And when I become a middle schooler,

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:39.620
Onee-sama will buy me one that is just as fancy as hers!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.030
Hey, you should listen when someone is talking to you! What are you doing?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:47.810
I forgot how you’re supposed to turn it off. What did the manual to do?

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.560
You don’t know how to do that?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.280
You hold this button down for a few seconds.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.240
Ginko-chan, you’re amazing! Thanks!{is it just me or does asu’s voice sound… um… huskier than usual in this episode? Maybe she should lay off the testosterone pills}

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.620
I’m always watching my sister, so I know all about this kind of thing!

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.520
If you have anything else that you don’t understand, just ask me for help.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.120
Okay, thanks! See you later.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.880
How lucky… a cell phone.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.660
Asu didn’t call today, eh?

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.680
I wonder if I should call her.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.150
Onee-chan hasn’t called yet, eh?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.310
Maybe I should call her.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.990
No, no, that’d be wasteful!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:45.990
<i>Wait a minute, maybe a time will come when we’ll really need to use these.</i>

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:51.630
<i>If I call now when there’s nothing big to talk about and those minutes get used up…</i>

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.660
How come you won’t use it? You should just call her if you want.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.880
Yeah, I guess you’re right.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.690
<i>Maybe this is what they mean by “a poor person’s mentality”.{貧乏性 【びんぼうしょう】 (n) destined to poverty; parsimonious spirit; tendency to be frugal; poor person’s mentality (e.g. inability to relax)}</i>

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.920
We’ve already had them for a week, huh?

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:16.840
Yeah.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:19.530
But we haven’t even used them yet.{well, TECHNICALLY, it should be "we never used them after that one time" but EH}

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.420
Yeah.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.900
If we let the three months just pass by like this…

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.680
That’d just be an even bigger waste, right?

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.800
Okay! From now on, let’s use them more freely!{BUT KYOU THIS SPELLS CERTAIN DOOM FOR YOUUUUUUUUUU}

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.010
S-Sure.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.480
We shouldn’t be {flagrantly}wasteful with them, of course—just in case something happens.{y u do dis 2 meh, brane}

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:43.620
Onee-chan, if you put it that way, we’ll just spend another week without using them at all.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.020
I guess you’re right.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.880
The evening papers…

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.780
I have to wake up, get out there, and try my best!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.340
Power on!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.140
Yamada-san!

00:09:59.140 --> 00:09:59.910
Yes?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.480
Can you give me a hand, please?{lol idiom}

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:02.580
Sure!

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:24.200
<i>Onee-chan isn’t answering, even though school’s already over.</i>

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.540
<i>I wonder if something could have happened.</i>

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.800
Ah, Ginko-chan.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.810
So you finally worked up the nerve to use it, eh?{I like the scaredy-cat implication, but the phrasing leaves a lot to be desired}

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:36.340
Yeah, Onee-chan and I decided that we should use them a little more freely.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:40.950
I wanted to ask her whether she would prefer curry or meat and potato stew for dinner tonight, but…{肉ジャガ 【にくジャガ】 (n) meat and potato stew}

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.670
Both dishes have the same ingredients.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:48.790
Oh yeah, Ginko-chan, if you want to call us, go right ahead, okay?

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.160
Your phone numbers…

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.250
Sure, if I feel like it.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:58.680
<i>Anyway, what could have happened to Onee-chan?</i>

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.970
<i>She’s been really tired, so I’m pretty worried.</i>

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:08.980
Our only goal is to make it to
the store-closing-sale on time.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:08.980
Half Price!

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:08.980
50% Off

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:17.480
On payday, we can have a luxurious
dinner with three side dishes.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.480
You can’t reach her?

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.450
Yeah, that’s strange, isn’t it…

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.380
Is there a signal?

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:30.090
I don’t have any idea.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.480
It was able to connect to her back at home.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.420
Well then,

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.840
let me give my sister a call to check if it works.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.180
Come on, let me give it a try.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:44.760
H-Hey.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.280
Hello?

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.520
Onee-sama, it’s Ginko.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.590
Yes, sorry to be calling you so suddenly.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.060
Is everything okay with you at the moment?

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:06.250
Yes, yes. Oh, is that so, Onee-sama?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.760
I heard it was won from a
shopping district raffle, yes.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.140
<i>That’s amazing.</i>

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.960
I think it was the third prize.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.140
Yes.{Jesus fuck she shouts these with an unnatural vigor}

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:16.660
<i>If only I could be that carefree on the phone, too.</i>

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.190
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.540
Yes!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.380
Yes, thank you very much.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:20.800
Yes.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.880
<i>This isn’t the time for a long conversation!</i>

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.520
Ah, um, Ginko-chan.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:28.860
If you have a long conversation
like this on my phone,

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:32.740
um, the 3000 yen limit will get all used up, so…{this conversation started when she hit the button to call her sister at precisely 0:11:53.796, according to the scenechange when kinko’s phone ringtone is heard. Asu starts saying this (presumably having fully formed the thought before starting speaking), at precisely 0:12:38.950. This gives a total conversation time (at this point), of 0:00:45.154 (assuming I did my math right). TIL: 3k円 is worth less than a minute of phone time.}

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:34.140
You’re not even listening.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:34.990
Um…

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:39.090
Yes, that’s right, Onee-sama. And then, I…

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.780
<i>Oh yeah… Onee-chan has been so tired lately,</i>

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.820
<i>she probably wouldn’t be up for a long conversation anyway.</i>

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.880
Ah, yes.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:54.410
<i>Ginko-chan, it’s good that you can have a full conversation like this.</i>

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.920
Missed Call

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.930
Yamada-san, thank you.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:57.920
Sure!

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.880
Hm, what’s this?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.740
Missed Call

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.720
Ah, I missed a call.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.360
It’s from Asu!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.580
What? It’s busy?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.080
Okay. That’s the tissue paper from the shopping district?{alternate translation: kleenex}

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.210
Okay.

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:17.710
Uh, yes.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.760
You turn the corner at the cigarette store, right?

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:21.880
Hey, um…

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:25.600
Yes, I’ll do just that!

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.780
Well then, goodbye for now, Onee-sama.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:29.810
Thanks.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:33.870
Missed Call

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:34.000
Missed Call

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:34.120
Missed Call

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:34.160
Missed Call

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:34.250
Missed Call

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:34.370
Missed Call

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:34.500
Missed Call

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:34.620
Missed Call

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:34.750
Missed Call

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:34.870
Missed Call

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.000
Missed Call

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:35.120
Missed Call

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:35.250
Missed Call

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:35.370
Missed Call

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.170
Onee-chan called, eh?

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:44.630
It’s from Asu!

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.950
Hello, Asu?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:49.930
Ah, Onee-chan—

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:53.730
Asu?

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.170
What happened, Asu?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.340
What’s wrong?

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.630
It cut out.

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:04.150
Looks like the battery died.

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:08.350
Um…

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:13.360
If you don’t properly charge it, the battery will die really fast, you know.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:21.990
<i>The number you have dialed is either not
currently turned on or is not within range of—</i>

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:22.800
South-East Newspaper

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:26.530
<i>It’s not connecting. What could be wrong?</i>

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.360
<i>Maybe something happened.</i>

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.980
<i>The number you have dialed is ei—</i>

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:34.980
<i>Ah, Onee-chan—{THE SOUND OF RAPE}</i>

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.560
<i>Something must have happened.</i>

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.570
<i>At this time, she’s always in the shopping district.</i>

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:49.860
Excuse me! I’ll be right back!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.870
<i>I wonder what Onee-chan wanted to talk about.{So. This show, instead of creating actual drama that might serve as a means for character development and plot progression, creates horribly forced, contrived drama in order to create "a moment of relief", in which the characters realize everything was okay. Well, at least it’s consistent.}</i>

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.300
<i>She looked pretty drowsy when she left this morning.{because groggy makes me think of hangovers. Kyou may be many things, but episodes 1-8 have lead me to believe that a drunkard is not one of them.}</i>

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:05.170
<i>Maybe she started feeling sick?</i>

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:11.340
Say, if you want to recharge the battery, my house has—

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.890
Huh? Where did she go?

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:18.270
<i>By this time, she should be
at the newspaper office.{newspaper outpost}{HA HA HA, WHAT ANOTHER SILLY MISUNDERSTANDING WHERE THEY BOTH GO TO WHERE THEY EXPECT THE OTHER TO BE BUT THEY AREN’T THERE BECAUSE THEY’VE GONE TO FIND EACH OTHER. THIS IS WHAT I CALL QUALITY SCRIPTWRITING.}</i>

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:23.170
Oh, Kyou-chan? Now that you mention it, she doesn’t seem to be here, does she?{POST MASTER GENERAL KAICHO SAMA}

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:26.240
She’s not here? Do you mean she never came?

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.130
Hey, boss! What should we do with this?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.450
Ah, I’ll be right there.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.240
Um…

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:34.660
Onee-chan… If she did really get collapse, she could be anywhere.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:39.000
You know, now that I think about it, Kyou-chan was here just a while a—

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.710
And now she’s gone.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:45.040
Oh, Asu-chan? No, I haven’t seen her yet today.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.210
Is that so?{Alternate translation: I doubt what you are saying because I don’t want it to be true because of the implications it has that the worst I feared has happened so I will desperately ask for assurance just in case you forgot that you saw her even though that is very unlikely seeing how you don’t seem to be suffering from senile dementia… HEY I JUST THOUGHT OF AN EPISODE WHERE A GUY WITH SENILE DEMENTIA FORGETS ABOUT ONE OF THEM AND THEN LIKE THEY LOSE EACH OTHER AND GET ALL DESPERATE AND THEN EVENTUALLY FIND EACH OTHER AND IT WAS ALL JUST A SILLY MISUNDERSTANDING. WE CAN GET THIS SHOW UP FOR A SECOND SEASON, I BET! I’LL EVEN SCRIPTWRITE FOR IT AND EVERYTHING!}

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.920
Now that you mention it, she’s usually here by now, isn’t she?

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.090
Here you go! Thank you!

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.140
Huh?

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:58.160
<i>This is strange. Asu wouldn’t purposefully hang up on me like that.</i>

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.880
<i>No way!</i>

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:01.190
<i>Was she kidnapped?!{Yes, because broke 9 year olds are prime suspects for kidnapping… now that I think about it, I guess asia does have a fairly large child prostitution thing going on.}{誘拐【ゆうかい】(n,vs) abduction; kidnapping; kidnaping;}</i>

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:11.030
<i>Onee-chan, where could you be?</i>

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:15.490
<i>Maybe she wasn’t feeling
well so she went back home.{THE DARK BACKGROUND AND MUSIC ARE ADDING TO THE TENSION}</i>

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.840
<i>—not within range of reception or—</i>

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:19.950
<i>Asu!</i>

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.000
Onee-chan!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.350
<i>The number you have—{OMG PANICK TAIMU}</i>

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:36.550
Come on!{this is some like dramatic 80s music}

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.610
<i>Onee-chan, Onee-chan, where are you?!</i>

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.110
<i>Onee-chan!</i>

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.070
<i>Onee-chan!</i>

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:51.410
<i>Onee-chan!</i>

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.240
<i>Onee-chan!{Do we really need to translate this?}</i>

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:58.660
Come on! Now that we have cell phones, how come they won’t work at a time like this?!{If you didn’t seriously see this coming from, like, before you even started watching this series, there is no hope for you.}

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.370
Onee-chan!{the benefits of living in a small town}

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:03.830
Asu!{Jesus fucking Christ this is like the goddamn first episode all over again}

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:06.640
Asu!!{MOAR EXCLAMATION POINTS FOR MORE DORAMA}

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:21.760
Onee-chan!

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.680
Asu!

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.510
Onee-chan!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:27.870
Asu!

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:31.590
Thank goodness! You didn’t collapse after all.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:35.890
The same goes for you. You weren’t kidnapped.{this needs to be changed somehow}

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.540
Thank goodness.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.230
Onee-chan.

00:17:57.190 --> 00:18:01.470
Really? The reason I couldn’t connect was because the battery died?

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.440
Yeah, there was a lot that happened.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:08.990
Same here. It was just because of bad timing that I wasn’t there to answer your call.

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:12.980
In the end, it was all by chance, but it sure wore us out.{oh fuck 9 year olds don’t talk like this OH WELL}

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.740
For sure.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:19.510
Oh, on that topic, what was it that you called about the first time?

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:26.820
I just wanted to ask if you would prefer curry or meat and potato stew for dinner tonight.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.640
Is that really all?

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.930
Sorry.

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.320
Meat and potato stew sounds great.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:38.960
Okay.

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:42.260
Who could that be?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.360
Hello?

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.160
Oh, she’s right here.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.410
Ginko-chan?

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:51.340
<i>It seems that you managed
to find your sister, right?</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.440
Yeah.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.580
<i>That’s great. I was worried.</i>

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:57.640
<i>Um, well…</i>

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.570
<i>I’m sorry for using up your phone’s battery!</i>

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.740
<i>I hope I didn’t end up causing too much trouble.</i>

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:07.260
No, you didn’t.

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:11.980
<i>Anyway, I’m also going to get my own cell phone!{remember, kids, these girls are in the 4th grade. THE WHORES GONNA BE SEXTING NAKED PICTURES OF THEMSELVES TO THEIR CLASSMATES JUST FOR ATTENTION. AREN’T YOU JEALOUS}</i>

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.660
I see. That’s great.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.290
Well then, see you tomorrow.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.380
<i>See you.</i>

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.490
Ginko-chan said she’s getting a cell phone too.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.680
That’s good.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:22.380
Yeah.

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.560
O-Onee-chan… the evening newspaper route!

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:31.060
You even still have the bicycle they lent you.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.520
Anyway, do your best!

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.470
I’ll make delicious stew for you!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:46.430
Onee-chan, are you all right?

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:48.440
I’m fine, I’m fine.

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:57.460
Oh, I forgot to tell Asu how good the fried eggs were this morning.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.670
Hello, Onee-chan?

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:06.980
<i>Ah, Asu, you know…</i>

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.140
What is it? Is something the matter?

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.640
<i>Are you feeling—</i>

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.890
<i>The fried eggs you made for breakfast were excellent!</i>

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:17.550
<i>That’s it.</i>

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:20.110
<i>That’s all I wanted to tell you, Asu.</i>

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:24.080
Thanks. Not just for this morning’s breakfast but for every single one, Asu.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:28.410
Don’t push yourself too much, Onee-chan.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.440
<i>It didn’t happen immediately,</i>

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:38.750
<i>but I eventually decided that these phones were a present from our mom in heaven.</i>

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>I got the feeling that I was being told, “It’s okay to relax a bit”,</i>

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:48.680
<i>from both mom and Asu.</i>

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.640
Alright! Giving it another shot?

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.720
Hah, you two. This has to be the 50th time in a row that you’ve tried.

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:59.480
You’re obviously after something.
What is it you want so badly?

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.700
The third prize: the cell phones.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:05.940
Onee-sama, we’re already out of raffle tickets.

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:09.090
If that’s the case, go buy some things to earn more.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:09.940
Yes.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:13.500
Mr. Attendant, prepare for our return.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:19.100
<i>Onee-sama, thank you for allowing me to have a cell phone.</i>

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:20.270
<i>But…</i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.800
<i>Just buying it the normal way would definitely be cheaper.</i>

